id:"p49", num:49, title:"C++ and Rust: Modern Systems Programming", short:"C++ & Rust",
tagline:"Take the C you already know and climb two ladders out of it: modern C++, where ownership is a convention that types and sanitizers enforce, and Rust, where ownership is a rule the compiler proves. Real toolchains, real error messages, real measurements — and an honest answer to which one to use.",
prereq:"Domain 15 Systems Programming is required: C, pointers and pointer arithmetic, the stack and the heap, malloc/free and ownership discipline, undefined behavior, the compile–assemble–link pipeline, ELF and GDB. Domain 13 (data structures and Big-O) is strongly recommended for Modules 2 and 6. This domain builds on C rather than re-teaching it. All labs run on your own Linux machine, VM or WSL2 with free toolchains (g++/clang++, CMake, gdb/lldb, sanitizers, rustup/cargo).",
